- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sopinvokegraph.html
- Summary (EN): SOP Invoke Graph runs a geometry SOP graph on incoming Copernicus (COP) inputs. It converts those inputs into geometry and passes them to the graph's inputs.
- Résumé (FR) : SOP Invoke Graph exécute un graphe de SOP géométrie sur des entrées COP, et désigne ses entrées et sorties par des groupes de points ordonnés.

- Inputs meaning: ["graph: the geometry graph defining the block to invoke, often generated by an Attribute from Parameters SOP", "input#: geometry for each corresponding graph input, following the node's Inputs setting"]

- Key parameters: ["Input Group: ordered point group selecting the nodes of the graph that act as inputs", "Inputs: number of inputs the graph accepts", "Output Group: ordered point group selecting the nodes of the graph that act as outputs", "Outputs: number of outputs the graph produces", "Unload Behavior: Always (default, discards intermediate data), Never (caches), or Use Node's Flag"]

- Caveats: ["Geometry graphs cannot contain expressions or channels, so a node network cannot simply be converted into one", "Use parameter overrides to get the same functionality"]

